WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.923 --> 00:00:10.641 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Welcome to the Asia capitals, episode four of seven. First, I clear the chosen
names for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:11.317 --> 00:00:21.766 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Eight capitals of the eastern Mediterranean and the Middle East: the island of
Cyprus, the Levant coast, the Jordan, Jerusalem, the Tigris, and the two great
inland powers.

3
00:00:22.431 --> 00:00:25.705 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Nicosia into view.

4
00:00:28.613 --> 00:00:34.755 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Nicosia stands on the plain in the centre of Cyprus, the largest city on the
island.

5
00:00:35.404 --> 00:00:49.348 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Its Venetian walls of the 16th century form a star with eleven bastions, and
since 2008 Ledra Street, in its old town, has been a crossing point between
the two sides.

6
00:00:50.001 --> 00:01:00.102 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Nicosia as the walled city of eleven bastions, whose old street is a
crossing point between the two sides of the island.

7
00:01:00.782 --> 00:01:02.779 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Beirut into view.

8
00:01:06.919 --> 00:01:13.781 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Beirut stands on the coast of the Mediterranean in the west of Lebanon, on a
bay below the Mount Lebanon range.

9
00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:29.849 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
From an old word for "wells", its Roman school of law was one of the most
famous of the empire. Rebuilt after the civil war of 1975 to 1990, it lost
much of its port area to an explosion in 2020.

10
00:01:30.511 --> 00:01:39.300 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Beirut as the city of wells and of the empire's law school, rebuilt
after its civil war.

11
00:01:39.979 --> 00:01:42.533 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Damascus into view.

12
00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:52.621 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Damascus stands on the Barada river in the south-west of Syria, on the edge of
the Syrian desert.

13
00:01:53.280 --> 00:02:05.900 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The Umayyad Mosque, built in the early 8th century, is one of the oldest great
mosques in the world, and the Straight Street of the Acts of the Apostles
still crosses its old city.

14
00:02:06.558 --> 00:02:13.803 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Damascus as the oldest great mosque of Islam, and the street of the
Acts still crossing its old town.

15
00:02:14.555 --> 00:02:16.517 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Amman into view.

16
00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:32.767 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Amman stands on the hills of north-central Jordan, about 800 metres above the
level of the Dead Sea below it.

17
00:02:33.428 --> 00:02:42.472 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The Rabbath Ammon of the Bible; the Greeks called it Philadelphia, and a Roman
theatre for some 6,000 people is cut into a hill in its centre.

18
00:02:43.123 --> 00:02:49.520 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Amman as the Rabbath Ammon of the Bible, with a Roman theatre cut
into the hill in its middle.

19
00:02:50.218 --> 00:02:52.726 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Jerusalem into view.

20
00:02:58.052 --> 00:03:10.545 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Jerusalem stands in the hills between the Mediterranean coast and the Jordan
valley; Israel claims it as its capital and it is the administrative seat of
the Palestinian Authority.

21
00:03:11.195 --> 00:03:21.644 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
A city holy to Judaism, Christianity and Islam; the walls of its Old City were
built by the Ottoman sultan Suleiman the Magnificent in the 1530s.

22
00:03:22.298 --> 00:03:29.926 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Jerusalem as the holy city of three religions, whose status is one of
the most disputed questions in the world.

23
00:03:30.608 --> 00:03:32.605 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Baghdad into view.

24
00:03:38.241 --> 00:03:45.149 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Baghdad stands on the Tigris in the centre of Iraq, about a hundred kilometres
from the Persian Gulf.

25
00:03:45.801 --> 00:03:55.611 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Founded in 762 by the caliph al-Mansur as a round city, its House of Wisdom
was a great centre of learning in the Islamic golden age.

26
00:03:56.267 --> 00:04:04.533 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Baghdad as the round city of 762, with the Tigris through its centre
and the House of Wisdom.

27
00:04:05.227 --> 00:04:08.640 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Ankara into view.

28
00:04:11.798 --> 00:04:21.132 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Ankara stands on the Ankara river in the centre of Anatolia, in the middle of
Türkiye, about 300 kilometres from the sea.

29
00:04:21.784 --> 00:04:33.858 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
From Ancyra, Greek for "anchor". Atatürk made it the capital in 1923 over
Istanbul, deliberately choosing a small Anatolian town of 30,000 people.

30
00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:43.053 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Ankara as the anchor in the middle of Anatolia, chosen as capital in
1923 over Istanbul.

31
00:04:43.738 --> 00:04:46.466 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Tehran into view.

32
00:04:50.069 --> 00:04:57.441 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Tehran stands on the southern slope of the Alborz mountains in the north of
Iran, with ski slopes within an hour of the city.

33
00:04:58.093 --> 00:05:09.181 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The capital since 1786 under the Qajar dynasty, and its Azadi Tower, built in
1971, is the symbol of the city.

34
00:05:09.843 --> 00:05:17.088 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Tehran as the capital of 1786 below the Alborz, with ski slopes an
hour away.

35
00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:38.905 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Nicosia stands alone on Cyprus, then Beirut, Damascus and Amman run along the
Levant with Jerusalem among them. Baghdad sits on the Tigris, Ankara in
Anatolia, and Tehran below the Alborz.

36
00:05:39.568 --> 00:05:59.728 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the eleven bastions and the crossing street, the wells and the law
school, the oldest great mosque, the theatre cut into a hill, the holy city of
three religions, the round city of 762, the anchor chosen over Istanbul, and
the capital of 1786.
